Georgia entitled “Criminal Trespass ~ Meters” is added and shall read as set forth on Exhibit A attached hereto and incorporated herein.

- 1. It shall be unlawful for any person intentionally and without authority to, with respect to any service manufactured, sold, or distributed by the City of Mansfield:

A. injure or destroy any meter, pipe, conduit, wire, line, post, lamp, or other apparatus belonging to the City of Mansfield;

B. prevent a meter from properly registering the quantity of such service supplied;

C. in any way to interfere with the proper action of the City of Mansfield while engaged in the provision of such services;

D. divert any such services; or

E. use or cause to be used, without the consent of the City of Mansfield, any such service.

- 2. The property owner, legal tenant or person(s) noted on the utility account shall be held responsible for the violation of this section. A tampering fine of seven hundred and fifty dollars ($750.00) shall be assessed for each violation of Section 31-111(1).

3, The City of Mansfield reserves the right to prosecute in the accordance with established laws any violation of Section 31-1111).

- 4. If the City of Mansfield determines theft of service has occurred, it reserves the right to adjust the customer's current bill and the bills for the past six (6) months usage. If the approximate amount of service that was stolen cannot be reasonably determined, the customer's usage will be set at three (3) times the average volume.
